  "goodToKnow": "Der Sauerstoff is oxygen. German translates many element names: Wasserstoff (hydrogen, water substance), Stickstoff (nitrogen, suffocating substance), Kohlenstoff (carbon). Sauerstoff literally means sour substance, a loan translation of the Greek-based oxygen (acid-maker), since Lavoisier wrongly believed all acids contain it. Der Sauerstoffmangel is lack of oxygen. Der Stoff means substance or fabric."
